

* Definitions of Lojban words: please go to [http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/|jbovlaste], the Lojban dictionary project.
* Lojban Attitudinals: you can find a list here: [http://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Lojban/Attitudinals]
* Basic Information: about Lojban, you can read or download ((What Is Lojban?, The Book)), also known as the Level Zero book, edited by Nick Nicholas and John Woldemar Cowan.  If you want a somewhat shorter introduction to Lojban, try the ((Frequently Asked Questions About Lojban)) page or the ((About Lojban)) page. 
* Lojban for Beginners: [http://www.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/lojbanbrochure/lessons/book1.html]
* Complete Lojban Language: [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=The+Complete+Lojban+Language&bl]
* Lojban Community or to use Lojban more effectively, please look at the ((Lojban Resources)) page.
* Mailing List: [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/]
* IRC: irc.freenode.net #lojban
* if you have a minute tell us how you first heard of Lojban ((Lojban: first time))
* If you are still having trouble finding something on this site, please use the ((Popular Pages)) page, or use the search menu at the upper left.

* If you are looking for information about the Logical Language Group, Inc., please go to the ((The Logical Language Group|Logical Language Group)) page.
* You can change the appearance of the site by selecting "MyTiki" (from the small menu) and selecting the image of the wrench and screwdriver.